Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:41:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 54/59] Ablation A4 replaces the index sink so no heartbeat
 path can repopulate the index

A4 patched only holder.embedded._heartbeat_stats, one of three feeders of OrgService.holder_heartbeat; the raw transport beat and the shutdown beat bypass it, so the term index flickered back every minute and was full at stop, and G8 (which reads the final coord.db) saw 112/112. A4 now replaces hypergraph.upsert_entity_index_sync and upsert_term_index_sync, the sinks every index write goes through (including the revoke / opt-out withdrawal): both return 0 and write nothing, whichever feeder delivers the beat.
Live-call counters (entity_index_calls, term_index_calls, entities_suppressed, terms_suppressed) go to run_manifest ablation_calls like A5's. Tests cover the embedded, transport and shutdown beats and the withdrawal helper, restore, and G8 failing on the resulting coord.db.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
